  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- After Spinna and Aladdin, the reviewer lists a new Krasno tune that seems familiar to them [6]\n- One in Seven was the standout, in the reviewer's view [7]\n- The reviewer singles out the Spinna into Aladdin segment on track 3 [8]\n- Track 7 has Krasno singing lead and Alan on backup vocals, not Neal [9]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **soulive2006-03-17t01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n- **soulive2006-03-17t08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [12]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2006-03-17.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 12 songs; 77 min; rated 4/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: The arena mix was poor, with too much bass and the keyboards hard to hear; The mix was pretty bad [7][9]\n- **soulive2006-03-17.flac24**: source not stated; 12 songs; 77 min [2]\n- **soulive2006-03-17.km184.flac16**: source not stated; 7 songs; 76 min; rated 4.5/5 by 4 [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The performance was part of the snoe.down event, and this reviewer was seeing the band for the first time [4]\n- The band played as a trio on this night, and the reviewer was glad to hear them back in that form [5]\n- The band played as a trio without horns, and the reviewer misses their older trio-only material [6]\n- Krasno struggled with his talk box throughout the night [7]\n- The show was a fun setting where the band shared the bill with other noted musicians [9]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2006-03-17.flac16**: taped by Jon Merin; transferred by Jon Merin; source: Schoeps MK41(DINA)->KC5->CMC6->V3->Tascam HD-P2 (24/96) [1]\n- **soulive2006-03-17.flac24**: taped by Jon Merin; transferred by Jon Merin; source: Schoeps MK41(DINA)->KC5->CMC6->V3->Tascam HD-P2 (24/96) [2]\n- **soulive2006-03-17.km184.flac16**: taped by Rob Clarke; transferred by Rob Clarke; source: Neumann KM184> Oade w-mod UA-5 (44.1 kHz)> optical> JB3 [3]",
